I performed detailed reconnaissance on networkwalks.com using six Kali Linux tools.
Key findings include:
WHOIS: Registrar = GoDaddy, privacy enabled, HostGator nameservers.
WhatWeb: WordPress 7.x, WP Download Manager plugin, Apache server, exposed REST API.
nslookup: Domain resolves to 192.232.216.135.
curl -I: Revealed headers, cookies, caching, and /wp-json/ endpoint.
wafw00f: Site is protected by ModSecurity (SpiderLabs) WAF.
dnsrecon: DNSSEC disabled, MX records, SPF/TXT records, SRV autodiscovery entries.
Why this matters
Shows publicly exposed information attackers can use.
Helps defenders understand their attack surface.
Reveals DNS, hosting, and technology stack details.
